{"title":"Roman numerals","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Roman_numerals&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p><p>1 - <b>I</b> <i>(unus)</i>\n</p><p>5 - <b>V</b> <i>(quinque)</i>\n</p><p>10 - <b>X</b> <i>(decem)</i>\n</p><p>50 - <b>L</b>\n</p><p>100 - <b>C</b> <i>(centum)</i>\n</p><p>500 - <b>D</b>\n</p><p>1000 - <b>M</b> <i>(mille)</i>\n</p><p>Numbers are written as combinations of letters. Letters are written from biggest to smallest value. Instead of writing IIII for 4, IV is used. To \"subtract,\" a smaller-value letter is placed before a larger-value letter. This done to make numbers smaller (e.g. IX instead of VIIII).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Roman_numerals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: History\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The ancient Romans developed a numeration system 3000 years ago. This system, now known as Roman numerals, lasted several centuries as the main numeration system. Today, Roman numerals are still used, but not as much as they were 3000 years ago.\n</p><p><br />\nYou can also add a line on top to multiply the number by 1,000.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Examples\">Examples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Roman_numerals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Examples\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>513 - DXIII\n</p><p>99 - IC\n</p><p>2006 - MMVI\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Roman_numerals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_systems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Number systems (page does not exist)\">Number systems</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017204439\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.016 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 16/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 283/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.573      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.573      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4027:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017204439 and revision id 104905. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}